@page
@model KopiCinta.Pages.CoffeeBlessingsKomunitasModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Coffee Blessings Komunitas";
}

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">

        <div class="back-top reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Community">← Back </a>
        </div>

        <!-- HERO -->
        <div class="kbi-hero reveal">
            <div class="kbi-hero-text">
                <p class="eyebrow">Community & Outreach</p>
                <h2>Coffee Blessings 2.0</h2>
                <p>
                    Sharing love, together — creating a space where people can come,
                    sit, connect, and feel welcomed through simple, meaningful moments.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-hero-image">
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/blessings-komunitas-hero.jpg">
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 1 -->
        <div class="kbi-section reveal">
            <div class="kbi-slider" data-kbi-slider>
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/coffee-komunitas-1.jpg" class="kbi-slide active">
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/coffee-komunitas-2.jpg" class="kbi-slide">
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/coffee-komunitas-3.jpg" class="kbi-slide">

                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn prev" data-prev>‹</button>
                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn next" data-next>›</button>
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-text">
                <h3>A Table for Everyone</h3>
                <p>
                    Not every act of giving requires us to go far.
                    Sometimes, it begins by simply creating a space
                    and allowing people to come, sit, and feel welcomed.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Through Coffee Blessings 2.0, we tried to hold a space like that—
                    simple, yet meaningful.
                </p>
                <p>
                    We invited different local communities from Akar Tuli, Harapan Ummat,
                    SpeakUp, Kasih Baca, to Islamic Disability Center.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Not as guests, but as part of the same story—
                    sitting at the same table, without distance, without roles,
                    just people meeting each other as they are.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 2 -->
        <div class="kbi-section reverse reveal">
            <div class="kbi-slider" data-kbi-slider>
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/coffee-sarapan-1.jpg" class="kbi-slide active">
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/coffee-sarapan-2.jpg" class="kbi-slide">
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/coffee-sarapan-3.jpg" class="kbi-slide">

                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn prev" data-prev>‹</button>
                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn next" data-next>›</button>
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-text">
                <h3>A Morning to Share</h3>
                <p>
                    The day began with a shared breakfast through
                    <em>Sarapan Pagi by Harmoni</em>.
                </p>
                <p>
                    In between the meals and conversations that slowly unfolded,
                    something quietly made its presence felt—love.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Not in a grand way, but enough to soften the space.
                </p>
                <p>
                    In that moment, coffee became a bridge.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 3 -->
        <div class="kbi-section reveal">
            <div class="kbi-slider" data-kbi-slider>
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/coffee-latte-1.jpg" class="kbi-slide active">
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/coffee-latte-2.jpg" class="kbi-slide">
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/coffee-latte-3.jpg" class="kbi-slide">

                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn prev" data-prev>‹</button>
                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn next" data-next>›</button>
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-text">
                <h3>Coffee as a Bridge</h3>
                <p>
                    Served through live latte art by Alif, one of our Deaf baristas,
                    each cup carried more than just taste.
                </p>
                <p>
                    There was a process behind it—a story being poured.
                    About the journey, about courage,
                    and about how small details can hold meaning.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 4 -->
        <div class="kbi-section reverse reveal">
            <div class="kbi-slider" data-kbi-slider>
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/coffee-growth-1.jpg" class="kbi-slide active">
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/coffee-growth-2.jpg" class="kbi-slide">
                <img src="/images/BlessingsKomunitas/coffee-growth-3.jpg" class="kbi-slide">

                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn prev" data-prev>‹</button>
                <button type="button" class="kbi-slide-btn next" data-next>›</button>
            </div>

            <div class="kbi-text">
                <h3>Because Love Grows When Shared</h3>
                <p>
                    We believe love does not always need to be big to matter.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Sometimes, it lives in the time we choose to give,
                    in the attention we hold,
                    and in the warmth that comes naturally.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Through Coffee Blessings 2.0, we were not only sharing coffee—
                    we were sharing space, moments, and something
                    that cannot always be put into words.
                </p>
                <p>
                    And from there, we are reminded that love always finds its way to grow
                    as long as it is shared.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="detail-back reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Community" class="btn btn-secondary">← Back to Community & Outreach</a>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>